6. WHAT THE BARRIER DOES (implementation summary)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- One fresh NO_OP per read, appended in the term read before append; no
  coalescing and no reuse of another read's NO_OP.
- Non-leader: failed future with NotLeaderException(leaderHint); no append.
- Append NotLeader -> NotLeaderException; StorageFailure/runtime error ->
  ReadUnavailableException; never a barrier.
- After Accepted(index, term): awaitIndex(index), then re-verify isLeader(),
  currentTerm()==term, termAt(index)==term, commitIndex()>=index. Any mismatch
  fails the read; no ReadBarrierResult is produced.
- Finite timeout > 0 required; timeout<=0 throws IllegalArgumentException.
  Late completion is ignored because each pending read settles exactly once
  (AtomicBoolean CAS).
- onLeadershipLost() fails all pending reads with NotLeaderException.
- No DB access, no commit/apply computation, no RaftState mutation. Pending set
  is concurrent and no lock is held while calling Port/AppliedAwaiter.
- Deliberate deviation from the sheet's output file: the implementation lives in
  the new RaftReadBarrier.java instead of RaftReplicationService.java, exactly as
  allowed by plan 1.3. RaftReplicationService.java is unchanged.

