7. REAL GREP RESULTS FOR PLAN 1.6 ("Chua lam")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A) RaftReadBarrier is not wired to NodeMain/handlers:
   grep -rn "RaftReadBarrier" backend-node/src/main/java
   -> only RaftReadBarrier.java itself (class declaration + constructor).
   NodeMain only declares parameters of type BookingRequestHandler.ReadBarrier
   (NodeMain.java lines 83, 116); it never constructs RaftReadBarrier.

B) NodeMain explicitly refuses reads/writes that are not wired:
   NodeMain.java lines 61-65:
     "Raft read barrier is not wired"
   NodeMain.java lines 100-104:
     "Leader majority commit/apply is not wired"

C) No runtime caller advances commit or applies committed entries on the Leader:
   grep -rn "\.advance\(\)|applyCommitted\(" backend-node/src/main/java
   -> WriteAvailabilityPolicy.tryAdvanceCommit() calls commitAdvancer.advance()
      (definition only); grep for "tryAdvanceCommit" finds no caller in main.
   -> RaftStateMachineApplier.applyCommitted() is only called inside its own
      class; grep for "RaftStateMachineApplier" in main finds only its own file.
   -> RaftStateMachineApplier is therefore not registered as a CommitListener in
      production NodeMain/ElectionRuntime.

D) No Leader NO_OP on becomeLeader:
   grep -rn "noOp|NO_OP|becomeLeader" backend-node/src/main/java
   -> RaftLogEntry.noOp factory exists; BookingCommand.NoOp / NO_OP handling
      exists in state machine and bridge; CandidateElection/ RaftState only
      perform becomeLeader(peers). No append of a Leader no-op entry on election.

E) Production RaftLogEntry -> BookingCommand codec DOES exist now:
   RaftApplyAdapter.decodeCommand(RaftLogEntry) at RaftApplyAdapter.java:381
   handles BOOK_TICKET, CANCEL_TICKET and NO_OP (line 404). This corrects the
   plan's earlier assumption. What is still missing is wiring: RaftApplyAdapter
   is not constructed by NodeMain/ElectionRuntime, so the codec is not on the
   runtime path.

F) Authoritative read handlers do not use the barrier:
   GetSeatsHandler.java routes the request to the Leader and then reads
   BookingService directly; it never calls ReadBarrier.appendAndAwaitNoOp.
   grep -rn "ReadBarrier|appendAndAwaitNoOp" backend-node/src/main/java/vn/nhom6/railway/networking
   -> only NodeMain parameter declarations, no handler usage.
   GetRequestResultHandler (booking) also does not take a ReadBarrier.

G) End-to-end read over TCP through TV3 handlers is therefore BLOCKED, not
   silently skipped: the handler does not invoke the barrier and NodeMain
   supplies a barrier that throws ReadUnavailableException("... not wired").

