9. HONESTY LIMITS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- The 2 integration tests use FakeNetwork/real in-JVM PersistentRaftNode and a
  manual scheduler. They do NOT prove 5 real nodes, real sockets, real crash or
  real election. G5 is not run here.
- The Leader commit/apply bridge used by those tests is harness-only. Production
  NodeMain still cannot produce CONFIRMED or a barrier result (section 7).
- `confirmedOnlyAfterCommitAndApply` proves the bridge/apply ordering in memory;
  it does not prove PostgreSQL durability of a booking (the JDBC applier tests
  are separate).
- Full suite includes 13 pre-existing environment-gated skips; 0 failures/errors.
- No claim is made that GET_SEATS/GET_REQUEST_RESULT/GET_TICKET_HISTORY now use
  the barrier end-to-end.

